course: dictionary
lesson: 5914
title: Marlin: a fast fish of the ocean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A marlin is a noun. It is the name of a thing, here a large fish. The words around it give you clues: «The fisherman hooked a giant marlin in the deep blue sea.» Giant, fisherman and sea tell you the marlin is big and lives in the ocean.
explain: Look for the body parts. «The marlin used its long pointed bill to catch smaller fish.» A bill is the long, spear-like nose of the fish. Its tall fin on its back is another clue that helps you picture it.
explain: Some words in front of marlin tell you which kind it is. Blue marlin, black marlin and striped marlin are three different kinds. Read the whole phrase, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A marlin is a large, fast ocean fish with a long pointed bill and a tall fin on its back.
fact: The bill is the long, spear-like nose of a marlin, and marlin use it to hunt smaller fish.
fact: Marlin are among the fastest fish in the sea.
fact: Blue marlin, black marlin and striped marlin are three kinds of marlin.
fact: In The Old Man and the Sea, a fisherman fights a giant marlin. In Finding Nemo, Marlin is a clownfish, not a real marlin, and «real clownfish families are stranger than the film».
exercise: «The fisherman hooked a giant marlin in the deep blue sea.» What is a marlin? | *A large, fast ocean fish | A kind of boat | A sort of seaweed | A small pond bird
exercise: «The marlin used its long pointed bill to catch smaller fish.» What is the bill? | *The long pointed nose of the fish | A fin on its back | A tail for swimming | A net the fisherman uses
exercise: Ravi sees a «striped marlin» on a sea trip. What does striped tell you? | That the fish is hiding | That the fish is very old | *Which kind of marlin it is | That the fish is sick
test: Marlin are among the fastest fish in the sea, so what can they do well? | Sleep all day | Grow very slowly | Fly through the air | *Swim very quickly
test: Which part is the tall part on a marlin's back? | *Fin | Tail | Bill | Scale
exam: Which sentence is true about a marlin? | It is a small bird that lives in trees | *It is a large fish with a long pointed bill | It is a fish that lives only in a small pond | It is a kind of tree that grows by a pond
